From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:27:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapback: fix long option table

The longopts array passed to getopt_long() had no terminating zero
entry, so parsing any long option read past the end of the array.

--name, --pidfile and --domain were also declared without argument
while their short forms require one, so e.g. "--domain 5" handed a
NULL optarg to strtoul().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tapback/tapback.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tapback/tapback.c b/tapback/tapback.c
index ee2076e4..407a5ce1 100644
--- a/tapback/tapback.c
+++ b/tapback/tapback.c
@@ -604,11 +604,12 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
             {"help", 0, NULL, 'h'},
             {"debug", 0, NULL, 'd'},
             {"verbose", 0, NULL, 'v'},
-            {"name", 0, NULL, 'n'},
-            {"pidfile", 0, NULL, 'p'},
-            {"domain", 0, NULL, 'x'},
+            {"name", 1, NULL, 'n'},
+            {"pidfile", 1, NULL, 'p'},
+            {"domain", 1, NULL, 'x'},
             {"nobarrier", 0, NULL, 'b'},
             {"noqueues", 0, NULL, 'q'},
+            {NULL, 0, NULL, 0},
         };
         int c;
 
